1. Inheritance — The Base Class & Its Variants
Instead of re-writing shared code (tags, running states, running hours) for every machine type (lathe, press, drill, grinder), Inheritance allows you to draw the parent family class once and specify only what makes each variant unique in child classes.
 * Base / Parent Class: Stores common attributes and methods shared across all machines.
 * Derived / Child Class: Inherits attributes/methods from the parent and adds or modifies its own specialized capabilities.
